.2B, in line with management's reaffirmed 2027 guidance and backed by a C$5.1B backlog. Operating margin should be near 11%, flat on 2026 (n2.r1).\n2. **Tarnwell Electric (TRNW):** Revenue should rise about 6%, driven by price increases. Operating margin should widen to 14% from 12% (n3.r1). Tarnwell is also taking share from Kelby in medium-voltage switchgear.\n3. **Braxen Cable (BRXC):** Revenue should grow about 2%, with flat volumes and growth coming only from pass-through pricing. Copper costs are up 18%, which squeezes margins, and earnings are expected to be flat (n4.r1).\n4. **Ostrand Meters (OSTM):** Revenue should rise sharply, with a smart-meter contract with Norvane Utilities adding about 20%. Margin should dip about one point as the Norvane rollout ramps up (n5.r1).\n5. **Kelby Switchgear (KLBS):** Revenue should fall about 5% as it loses share to Tarnwell. Restructuring should hold operating margin at 8% (n6.r1).\n\n**Overall:** Ostrand and Tarnwell look strongest on growth. Voltaris looks steady. Braxen is squeezed by copper costs. Kelby is the weakest on revenue, and its loss to Tarnwell is Tarnwell's gain.","ttft_ms":2181,"type":"result","duration_ms":27002,"uuid":"1d10df16-82e0-4477-b6cb-cd4adf80778d","ttft_stream_ms":1378,"time_to_request_ms":391,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":23,"system_prompt":56,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":31,"input_attachments":90,"input_hooks":9,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":16,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":37,"init_frame_send":9,"engine_pickup":7,"loop_entry":11,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":0,"autocompact":13,"request_announcements":30,"query_setup":1,"model_gates":8,"tool_schema_build":9,"message_normalization":8,"client_creation":15,"request_build":16},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":147,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":74,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":174,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":99,"process_rss_